# CR 500.4's own "every player" scope: as the turn's Cleanup ends
# (Game.onCleanupPhase, PhaseHandler.java:508-511) this turn's LandsPlayed
# resets to zero (expect.state has no landsplayed= line), ready for a land to be
# played again once a future turn reaches Main1. Main1 -> ... -> Cleanup is
# 9 advances, the 10th leaves Cleanup for the next turn's Untap; at Cleanup
# itself the land still counts as played this turn.
# TestCleanupResetsLandsPlayedForEveryPlayer (land_test.go) is the unit-level
# version of the same rule; this is its scenario-level counterpart.
startturn human
advance 3
playland human 1
advance 10
